The fast dispatch is UNREACHABLE from a reflection-built minitable, whatever
UPB_FASTTABLE is: upb/wire/decode.c:766 fires only when table_mask != -1, and
upb/mini_descriptor/decode.c:698,712 sets table_mask = -1 on every minitable it
builds. The fasttable entries come from protoc-gen-upb's UPB_FASTTABLE_INIT and
from nothing else. The runtime table_mask above is the proof, and the fast-parse
function count printed by gen/fetch_upb.sh is the proof that the code IS compiled
in when the define is set -- so the null result is a reachability fact, not a
build that silently did nothing.
